This component is additive work in the same Poincare research repository.

Thirteen reused proof/model files are byte-identical to research/collar-separation
at KunHcz/poincare-lean@d4d27d1b4d8c0d447ddf02df4999b35bb3118213.
They retain all earlier attribution and are not counted as new results here.

The new proofs use Mathlib's compact-set neighbourhood theorem, local
homeomorphisms, strict/C1 inverse function theorems, standard topology and
calculus. The inherited cap/separation chain uses the proved Hatcher
van Kampen surjectivity, not an unproved kernel-identification theorem.
Lean, Mathlib, Hatcher and the respective formalization authors retain their
mathematical and code credit. No dependent-library authorship is claimed by
the applicant merely because this repository is owned by that applicant.

The local contribution constructs and checks the uniform collar from the
pointwise data and connects genuine coordinate inverse-function input to the
existing separation/capping proof. It does not prove the necessary family
exists for every embedded sphere or complete the Poincare theorem.

Local Lean/Python code uses the included Apache License 2.0. Dependency source,
compiled caches, private paths and credentials are not redistributed. This
intermediate research component is not a complete-original-problem award
submission and makes no priority, solver-share or payment claim.
